; raise ... at Address[, Frame]: both must be pointers (as in Free Pascal);
; ExceptAddr takes no arguments and is a pointer.
; RUN: not %p3 --mode=objfpc -ferror-limit=0 -c %S/Inputs/raiseat/errors.pas -o %t.o 2>&1 | FileCheck %s
; CHECK: errors.pas:8:34: error: the address of a raised exception must be a pointer, not 'integer'
; CHECK: errors.pas:9:39: error: the frame of a raised exception must be a pointer, not 'real'
; CHECK: errors.pas:10:34: error: the address of a raised exception must be a pointer, not 'string'
; CHECK: errors.pas:10:37: error: the frame of a raised exception must be a pointer, not 'string of length 3'
; CHECK: errors.pas:12:5: error: assigning to 'integer' from incompatible type 'pointer'
; CHECK: errors.pas:13:8: error: 'ExceptAddr' expects 0 arguments
; CHECK-NOT: error:
;
; An address and a frame must follow `at` and its comma.
; RUN: not %p3 --mode=objfpc -ferror-limit=0 -c %S/Inputs/raiseat/syntax.pas -o %t.o 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=SYNTAX %s
; SYNTAX: syntax.pas:3:33: error: expected expression
; SYNTAX: syntax.pas:4:38: error: expected expression
; SYNTAX-NOT: error:
;
; ExceptAddr is predeclared only with --mode=objfpc; `at` is not reserved.
; RUN: %p3 -c %S/Inputs/raiseat/iso.pas -o %t.o
; RUN: %p3 --mode=tp -c %S/Inputs/raiseat/iso.pas -o %t.o
; RUN: %p3 --mode=objfpc -c %S/Inputs/raiseat/iso.pas -o %t.o
;
; The AST shows the address and the frame after the object.
; RUN: %p3 --mode=objfpc --emit-ast -o - %S/../run/raiseat.pas | FileCheck --check-prefix=AST %s
; AST:      RaiseStmt at <41:3>
; AST-NEXT:   NameRefExpr 'e' parameter : TObject <41:9>
; AST-NEXT:   NameRefExpr 'addr' parameter : pointer <41:14>
; AST-NEXT:   NameRefExpr 'frame' parameter : pointer <41:20>
